_KLIPPEE_PAGE = "<style>\n[hidden] { display: none !important; }\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 20px; font: 14px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--orca-fg, #202124); background: var(--orca-bg, #fff); }\nmain { max-width: 660px; margin: auto; } label { display: block; margin: 12px 0; }\ninput, select { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; padding: 9px; margin-top: 5px; font: inherit; color: inherit; background: var(--orca-bg, #fff); border: 1px solid var(--orca-border, #888); border-radius: 5px; }\nbutton { padding: 9px 14px; margin: 5px 6px 5px 0; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\nselect { width: 100%; padding: 8px; font: inherit; color: inherit; background: var(--orca-bg, #fff); }\nbutton:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: .6; } :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #2979ff; outline-offset: 2px; }\n#status { min-height: 24px; } li { margin: 6px 0; } .note { color: var(--orca-muted, #60656c); }\n</style>\n<main>\n<h1>Klippee</h1>\n<h2>Save to Klippee</h2>\n<p>Import enabled printer profiles and all custom process and filament profiles into your private library. Nozzle variants stay separate. Physical printers are linked optionally in Klippee.</p>\n<section id=\"connectedUploads\" hidden aria-label=\"Save using your connection\">\n<button id=\"reviewSavedLibrary\" type=\"button\">Review profile import</button>\n<button id=\"reviewSavedSetup\" type=\"button\">Review current setup</button>\n<p>Review each upload before confirming. Profile imports replace your library backup; setup saves add a new snapshot with all filament slots and unsaved edits. No printer actions are sent. Enable imports and saves for this installation in Klippee first.</p>\n</section>\n<div id=\"manualImport\"><p>In Klippee, open Orca Workspace and choose Import from OrcaSlicer to create a code. A saved-setup code captures only your current combination instead.</p>\n<label>Connection code<input id=\"code\" type=\"password\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" maxlength=\"2048\"></label>\n<button id=\"review\" type=\"button\">Review import</button></div>\n<section id=\"preview\" hidden aria-label=\"Setup review\">\n  <h2 id=\"printer\"></h2><p id=\"site\" class=\"note\"></p><ul id=\"selections\"></ul>\n  <details id=\"libraryReview\" hidden><summary id=\"libraryCount\"></summary><ul id=\"libraryProfiles\"></ul></details>\n  <p id=\"ancestry\"></p><p id=\"omitted\" class=\"note\"></p>\n  <p>Custom G-code is included. Review it for personal information before saving. No models or printer actions are sent.</p>\n  <label id=\"setupTitle\">Setup name<input id=\"title\" maxlength=\"120\"></label>\n  <button id=\"save\" type=\"button\">Save to Klippee</button><button id=\"cancel\" type=\"button\">Cancel</button>\n</section>\n<h2>Browse your Klippee library</h2>\n<p>In Klippee's Orca Workspace choose Browse library in OrcaSlicer. Paste the connection code once. This Orca installation stays connected after restarts until you disconnect it here or in Klippee. Browsing and restoring are always available. Imports and setup saves need the permission enabled in Klippee and your confirmation for each upload. Nothing syncs automatically.</p>\n<div id=\"libraryPairing\"><label>Library access code<input id=\"browseCode\" type=\"password\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" maxlength=\"2048\"></label>\n<button id=\"browseLibrary\" type=\"button\">Open library</button></div>\n<section id=\"libraryBrowser\" hidden aria-label=\"Klippee library\">\n  <p id=\"libraryAccess\" class=\"note\"></p>\n  <button id=\"reloadLibrary\" type=\"button\">Reload library</button><button id=\"disconnectLibrary\" type=\"button\">Disconnect library</button>\n  <label>Search saved profiles<input id=\"librarySearch\" type=\"search\"></label>\n  <label>Profile type<select id=\"libraryKind\"><option value=\"\">All profiles</option><option value=\"machine\">Printer profiles</option><option value=\"filament\">Custom filaments</option><option value=\"process\">Custom processes</option></select></label>\n  <label>Saved profile<select id=\"libraryProfile\" size=\"8\"></select></label>\n  <p id=\"browserProfileCount\" role=\"status\"></p><p id=\"libraryProfileDetails\"></p>\n  <button id=\"reviewLibraryProfile\" type=\"button\">Review selected profile</button>\n</section>\n<h2>Restore from a file</h2>\n<p>In Klippee, choose Export profile for OrcaSlicer on a library profile, or Export saved setup. Open the JSON file here to restore separate copies with their full inheritance.</p>\n<p>Your original presets, current selections, unsaved edits and models stay unchanged. Restoring again creates another set of copies. No printer actions are sent.</p>\n<label>Saved profile or setup file<input id=\"restoreFile\" type=\"file\" accept=\".json,application/json\"></label>\n<section id=\"restorePreview\" hidden aria-label=\"Restore review\">\n  <h3>Review the saved profile or setup</h3><ul id=\"restoreSelections\"></ul>\n  <p id=\"restoreAncestry\"></p>\n  <p>Custom G-code is included and can run when you later print. Only restore files you trust. Printer connection credentials are excluded.</p>\n  <button id=\"restore\" type=\"button\">Restore preset copies</button>\n</section>\n<section id=\"restoreResult\" hidden aria-label=\"Restored preset selections\">\n  <h3>Restored copies</h3>\n  <p>For an individual profile, select the listed copy in Prepare when needed. Your other selections and filament slots stay unchanged. For a complete setup, Orca requires manual selection after restore. Choose the printer first, then process, then each filament slot below. Add or remove filament slots to match this list. These names belong to the new copies. Keep or save any current edits if Orca asks.</p>\n  <ol id=\"restoredNames\"></ol>\n</section>\n<button id=\"checkRestore\" type=\"button\">Check last restore</button>\n<button id=\"cancelOperation\" type=\"button\" hidden>Cancel operation</button>\n<p id=\"status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n</main>\n<script>\n(() => {\n  const element = id => document.getElementById(id);\n  let waiting = false;\n  function busy(value) { waiting = value; for (const id of ['review', 'save', 'cancel', 'code', 'title', 'restoreFile', 'restore', 'checkRestore', 'browseCode', 'browseLibrary', 'reloadLibrary', 'disconnectLibrary', 'librarySearch', 'libraryKind', 'libraryProfile', 'reviewLibraryProfile', 'reviewSavedLibrary', 'reviewSavedSetup']) element(id).disabled = value; element('cancelOperation').hidden = !value; }\n  function selectionLabel(index) { return index === 0 ? 'Printer' : index === 1 ? 'Process' : 'Filament ' + (index - 1); }\n  let library = null;\n  const profileLabel = kind => ({machine: 'Printer profile', filament: 'Filament', process: 'Process'}[kind]);\n  function updateProfileDetails() {\n    const profile = library?.profiles.find(item => item.id === element('libraryProfile').value);\n    element('reviewLibraryProfile').disabled = waiting || !profile;\n    element('libraryProfileDetails').textContent = profile ? profileLabel(profile.kind) + (profile.nozzle ? ' · ' + profile.nozzle + ' mm nozzle' : '') + ' · Inherits from: ' + (profile.parent || 'No parent') + '. The complete ancestry will be restored as separate copies.' : '';\n  }\n  function filterProfiles() {\n    const selected = element('libraryProfile').value;\n    const query = element('librarySearch').value.trim().toLowerCase(), kind = element('libraryKind').value;\n    const profiles = (library?.profiles || []).filter(p => (!kind || p.kind === kind) && (p.name + ' ' + (p.nozzle || '')).toLowerCase().includes(query));\n    element('libraryProfile').replaceChildren(...profiles.map(p => {\n      const option = document.createElement('option'); option.value = p.id; option.textContent = profileLabel(p.kind) + ': ' + p.name; return option;\n    }));\n    if (profiles.some(p => p.id === selected)) element('libraryProfile').value = selected;\n    else if (profiles.length) element('libraryProfile').selectedIndex = 0;\n    element('browserProfileCount').textContent = profiles.length + ' of ' + (library?.profiles.length || 0) + ' saved profiles';\n    updateProfileDetails();\n  }\n  function showLibrary(value, origin) {\n    library = value; element('libraryBrowser').hidden = !value; element('libraryPairing').hidden = !!value; element('manualImport').hidden = !!value; element('connectedUploads').hidden = !value;\n    if (value) { element('libraryAccess').textContent = origin + (value.expiresAt ? ' · Read-only access until ' + new Date(value.expiresAt).toLocaleTimeString() : ' · Connected on this computer · ' + (value.uploadsEnabled ? 'Browsing, profile imports and setup saves enabled' : 'Read-only library access')) + '. Originals and active selections are kept.'; filterProfiles(); }\n  }\n  for (const [id, command] of [['reviewSavedLibrary', 'review_saved_library'], ['reviewSavedSetup', 'review_saved_setup']]) {\n    element(id).onclick = () => { element('preview').hidden = true; element('restorePreview').hidden = true; element('restoreResult').hidden = true; busy(true); orca.postMessage({command}); };\n  }\n  element('browseLibrary').onclick = () => { element('preview').hidden = true; element('restorePreview').hidden = true; element('restoreResult').hidden = true; busy(true); orca.postMessage({command: 'browse_library', code: element('browseCode').value}); };\n  element('reloadLibrary').onclick = () => { busy(true); orca.postMessage({command: 'reload_library'}); };\n  element('disconnectLibrary').onclick = () => orca.postMessage({command: 'disconnect_library'});\n  element('librarySearch').oninput = filterProfiles; element('libraryKind').onchange = filterProfiles;\n  element('libraryProfile').onchange = updateProfileDetails;\n  element('reviewLibraryProfile').onclick = () => {\n    if (!element('libraryProfile').value) return;\n    element('restorePreview').hidden = true; element('restoreResult').hidden = true; busy(true);\n    orca.postMessage({command: 'review_library_profile', profileId: element('libraryProfile').value});\n  };\n  element('cancelOperation').onclick = () => orca.postMessage({command: 'cancel'});\n  element('title').oninput = () => orca.postMessage({command: 'set_title', title: element('title').value});\n  element('restoreFile').onchange = async () => {\n    const file = element('restoreFile').files[0];\n    if (!file) return;\n    element('restorePreview').hidden = true; element('restoreResult').hidden = true; element('preview').hidden = true;\n    if (file.size > 600000) { element('status').textContent = 'Choose a Klippee profile or setup export smaller than 600 KB.'; return; }\n    busy(true); element('status').textContent = 'Validating saved setup…';\n    try { const text = await file.text(); element('restoreFile').value = ''; orca.postMessage({command: 'review_restore', text}); }\n    catch { busy(false); element('status').textContent = 'Could not read the setup file.'; }\n  };\n  element('restore').onclick = () => { busy(true); element('status').textContent = 'Restoring and verifying preset copies…'; orca.postMessage({command: 'restore'}); };\n  element('checkRestore').onclick = () => { busy(true); element('status').textContent = 'Checking selections and inheritance…'; orca.postMessage({command: 'check_restore'}); };\n  element('review').onclick = () => {\n    element('preview').hidden = true; busy(true); element('status').textContent = 'Reading your setup and checking the connection code…';\n    orca.postMessage({command: 'review', code: element('code').value});\n  };\n  element('save').onclick = () => {\n    busy(true); element('status').textContent = 'Saving setup…'; orca.postMessage({command: 'save', title: element('title').value});\n  };\n  element('cancel').onclick = () => { orca.postMessage({command: 'cancel'}); };\n  function render(message) {\n    if (!message) return;\n    if (message.command === 'working') { busy(true); element('status').textContent = message.text; return; }\n    busy(false);\n    if (message.command === 'error') { if (message.disconnected) showLibrary(null, ''); element('status').textContent = message.error; return; }\n    if (message.command === 'library_listed') {\n      element('browseCode').value = ''; showLibrary(message.library, message.origin); element('status').textContent = message.library.profiles.length ? 'Choose a profile to review before restoring copies.' : 'Your library is empty. Import profiles from Orca into Klippee first.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'restore_review') {\n      element('restoreSelections').replaceChildren(...message.selections.map((item, index) => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = (item.kind === 'machine' ? 'Printer' : item.kind === 'process' ? 'Process' : 'Filament' + (item.slot === null ? '' : ' ' + (item.slot + 1))) + ': ' + item.name + (item.dirty ? ' (captured unsaved changes)' : ''); return li;\n      }));\n      element('restoreAncestry').textContent = message.nodes + ' saved presets and their inheritance will be preserved.' + (message.profile ? ' The profile is restored from its saved settings.' : ' Captured edits become separate child presets.');\n      element('restorePreview').hidden = false; element('status').textContent = 'Review this saved profile or setup, then restore copies.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'restored') {\n      element('restorePreview').hidden = true;\n      element('restoredNames').replaceChildren(...message.names.map((name, index) => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li'); const label = document.createElement('label'); label.textContent = message.profile ? ({machine: 'Printer profile', process: 'Process', filament: 'Filament'}[message.kinds[index]]) : selectionLabel(index);\n        const input = document.createElement('input'); input.readOnly = true; input.value = name; input.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Restored ' + label.textContent); label.append(input); li.append(label); return li;\n      }));\n      element('restoreResult').hidden = false;\n      element('status').textContent = message.notice || (message.profile ? 'Profile and its full inheritance restored and verified. Select the new copy in Prepare when needed. Check last restore verifies it without changing selections.' : 'Preset copies restored and verified. Select all the listed presets, then choose Check last restore.');\n    } else if (message.command === 'profile_verified') {\n      element('status').textContent = 'Verified: the restored profile and all ' + message.nodes + ' presets in its inheritance chain match the saved copy. Your current selections are unchanged. Nothing was sent to the printer.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'restore_verified') {\n      element('status').textContent = 'Verified: the restored printer, process and all ' + message.slots + ' filament slots are selected. All ' + message.nodes + ' presets and their inheritance match the saved copy. Nothing was sent to the printer.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'connected') {\n      element('printer').textContent = 'Save to ' + message.data.printerName;\n      const profiles = message.profiles || [];\n      element('libraryReview').hidden = !profiles.length;\n      element('libraryCount').textContent = profiles.length + ' library profiles (including profiles not currently selected)';\n      element('libraryProfiles').replaceChildren(...profiles.map(item => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = (item.kind === 'machine' ? 'Printer profile' : item.kind === 'process' ? 'Process' : 'Filament') + ': ' + item.name; return li;\n      }));\n      element('save').textContent = profiles.length ? 'Import profiles to Klippee' : 'Save to Klippee';\n      element('setupTitle').hidden = !!profiles.length;\n      element('site').textContent = message.origin;\n      element('selections').replaceChildren(...message.selections.map(item => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li');\n        const label = item.kind === 'filament' ? 'Filament ' + (item.slot + 1) : item.kind === 'machine' ? 'Printer' : 'Process';\n        li.textContent = label + ': ' + item.name + (item.dirty ? ' (includes unsaved changes)' : ''); return li;\n      }));\n      element('ancestry').textContent = message.nodes + ' presets in the inheritance graph will be preserved.';\n      element('omitted').textContent = message.omittedKeys.length ? 'Connection/account fields excluded: ' + message.omittedKeys.join(', ') : 'No printer connection credentials detected.';\n      element('title').value = (message.selections[0].name + ' / ' + message.selections[1].name).slice(0, 120);\n      element('preview').hidden = false; element('status').textContent = 'Review this setup before saving.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'saved') {\n      element('preview').hidden = true; element('code').value = '';\n      element('status').textContent = message.data.library ? 'Profiles imported into your Klippee library. Your current setup and unsaved edits are included in the backup. Reload the library in Klippee to see the updated import.' : 'Saved to Klippee. Reload the library in Klippee to see the new saved setup.';\n    } else if (message.command === 'cancelled') {\n      element('preview').hidden = true; element('code').value = ''; element('browseCode').value = ''; showLibrary(message.library || null, message.origin || ''); element('status').textContent = message.notice || 'Disconnected locally. Revoke the code in Klippee to end its server access immediately.';\n      element('restorePreview').hidden = true;\n    }\n  }\n  orca.onMessage(message => {\n    if (message && message.command === 'state') {\n      for (const id of ['preview', 'restorePreview', 'restoreResult']) element(id).hidden = true;\n      showLibrary(message.library || null, message.browseOrigin || '');\n      if (message.view) render(message.view);\n      element('title').value = message.title || '';\n      busy(message.busy);\n      if (message.notice) element('status').textContent = message.notice;\n      else if (message.busy) element('status').textContent = message.progress || 'Working…';\n    } else render(message);\n  });\n  orca.postMessage({command: 'ready'});\n  setInterval(() => { if (waiting) orca.postMessage({command: 'poll'}); }, 100);\n})();\n</script>\n"

"""Native preset capture shared by the plugin and round-trip spike."""
from pathlib import Path
import json

FORMAT = "klippee-orca-setup/v1"
COLLECTIONS = {"machine": "printers", "process": "prints", "filament": "filaments"}
# Project/runtime inventory absent from the machine preset on native reload.
# Retain it in capture evidence, but do not treat it as a persistent setting.
RUNTIME_ONLY = {"extruder_nozzle_stats"}
IDENTITY_KEYS = {"printer_settings_id", "print_settings_id", "filament_settings_id"}


def canonical_value(key, value):
    # Native preset normalization inserts spaces between thumbnail descriptors;
    # the project loader does not. Compare the descriptor list, not whitespace.
    if key == "thumbnails" and isinstance(value, str):
        return ",".join(part.strip() for part in value.split(","))
    return value


def values(preset):
    result = {key: preset.config_value(key) for key in preset.config_keys()}
    if any(not isinstance(value, str) for value in result.values()):
        raise ValueError("Host returned a non-string configuration value")
    return result


def capture(bundle, library=False):
    """Copy live views immediately; capture saved ancestry and unsaved deltas.

    Never retain native Preset references across callbacks. Unknown source JSON
    fields survive in source_json, even when Orca does not expose them.
    """
    nodes = {}
    saved_presets = {}
    for kind, attribute in COLLECTIONS.items():
        collection = getattr(bundle, attribute)
        saved_presets[kind] = {collection.preset(index).name: collection.preset(index)
                               for index in range(collection.size())}

    def visit(kind, preset, collection, visiting=()):
        identity = kind + ":" + preset.name
        if identity in visiting:
            raise ValueError("Cyclic inheritance: " + identity)
        if identity in nodes:
            return identity
        config = values(preset)
        parent_name = config.get("inherits", "")
        parent_id = None
        if parent_name:
            parent = saved_presets[kind].get(parent_name)
            if parent is None:
                raise ValueError("Missing parent preset: " + parent_name)
            parent_id = visit(kind, parent, collection, visiting + (identity,))
        source = None
        source_path = Path(preset.file) if preset.file else None
        if source_path and source_path.is_file():
            # A present but unreadable/malformed file is an error, never silently
            # replace its metadata with a guessed representation.
            source = json.loads(source_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").lstrip("\ufeff"))
            if not isinstance(source, dict):
                raise ValueError("Preset file must contain a JSON object")
        nodes[identity] = {
            "kind": kind, "name": preset.name, "parent": parent_id,
            "saved": config, "source_json": source,
        }
        return identity

    selections = []

    def selected(kind, saved, edited, slot=None):
        collection = getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind])
        identity = visit(kind, saved, collection)
        current = values(edited)
        baseline = nodes[identity]["saved"]
        removed = set(baseline) - set(current)
        if removed:
            raise ValueError("Edited preset removed keys in " + kind + ": " + ", ".join(sorted(removed)))
        if current.get("inherits", "") != baseline.get("inherits", ""):
            raise ValueError("Changing the inheritance parent in memory is unsupported")
        selections.append({
            "node": identity, "slot": slot,
            "dirty": bool(edited.is_dirty), "effective": current,
            "changes": {key: value for key, value in current.items()
                        if value != baseline.get(key) and key not in RUNTIME_ONLY},
        })

    for kind in ("machine", "process"):
        collection = getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind])
        selected(kind, collection.get_selected_preset(), collection.get_edited_preset())
    filament_collection = bundle.filaments
    edited_filament = filament_collection.get_edited_preset()
    for slot, current in enumerate(bundle.current_filament_presets()):
        if current is None:
            raise ValueError("Missing filament in slot " + str(slot))
        # find_preset(), used by current_filament_presets(), can substitute the
        # live edit buffer. Only collection.preset(index) is a saved baseline.
        saved = saved_presets["filament"].get(current.name)
        if saved is None:
            raise ValueError("Missing saved filament: " + current.name)
        edited = edited_filament if saved.name == edited_filament.name else saved
        selected("filament", saved, edited, slot)
    snapshot = {"format": FORMAT, "nodes": dict(nodes), "selections": selections}
    if not library:
        return snapshot
    profiles = []
    for kind, presets in saved_presets.items():
        for preset in presets.values():
            custom = bool(preset.is_user())
            enabled = bool(preset.is_visible)
            # Compatibility with the current printer is deliberately irrelevant:
            # a filament for another nozzle/printer still belongs in the library.
            if not preset.is_default and (custom or (kind == "machine" and enabled)):
                profiles.append({"node": visit(kind, preset, getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind])),
                                 "custom": custom, "enabled": enabled})
    return {"format": "klippee-orca-library/v1", "nodes": nodes,
            "profiles": profiles, "current": snapshot}



"""Native restore planning and verification, shared with the disposable spike."""
from copy import deepcopy
import csv
import hashlib
import json
import re
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

PROFILE_FORMAT = "klippee-orca-profile/v1"

PRIVATE_KEY = re.compile(r"password|passwd|secret|token|api_?key|access_?code|printhost|print_host|host_type|authorization|^(setting_id|base_id|user_id)$", re.I)


def comparison_keys(actual, wanted):
    # Captures deliberately omit connection/account options. Orca reinstates
    # native defaults on load; those absent fields are outside the saved setup.
    return {key for key in (set(actual) | set(wanted)) - IDENTITY_KEYS - RUNTIME_ONLY
            if key in wanted or not PRIVATE_KEY.search(key)}


def validate_restore(document):
    """Validate an untrusted exported JSON file before planning any disk writes."""
    if not isinstance(document, dict):
        raise ValueError("Choose an exported Klippee setup JSON file.")
    snapshot = document.get("snapshot")
    if not isinstance(snapshot, dict) or snapshot.get("format") not in (FORMAT, PROFILE_FORMAT):
        raise ValueError("Unsupported Klippee setup file.")
    individual = snapshot["format"] == PROFILE_FORMAT
    nodes = snapshot.get("nodes")
    selections = snapshot.get("selections")
    if not isinstance(nodes, dict) or not 1 <= len(nodes) <= 128 or not isinstance(selections, list) or not (len(selections) == 1 if individual else 3 <= len(selections) <= 34):
        raise ValueError("Invalid setup size or filament slots.")

    def settings(value):
        return isinstance(value, dict) and len(value) <= 4096 and all(isinstance(k, str) and isinstance(v, str) for k, v in value.items())

    # Validate parent shapes first so ancestry walking never follows an unchecked value.
    for node in nodes.values():
        if not isinstance(node, dict) or "parent" not in node or node["parent"] is not None and not isinstance(node["parent"], str):
            raise ValueError("Invalid preset parent.")
    for identity, node in nodes.items():
        if not isinstance(node, dict) or node.get("kind") not in COLLECTIONS or not isinstance(node.get("name"), str) or not 1 <= len(node["name"]) <= 512 or identity != node["kind"] + ":" + node["name"]:
            raise ValueError("Invalid preset identity.")
        if not settings(node.get("saved")) or not (node.get("source_json") is None or isinstance(node["source_json"], dict)):
            raise ValueError("Invalid preset settings.")
        if "parent" not in node or node["parent"] is not None and not isinstance(node["parent"], str):
            raise ValueError("Invalid preset parent.")
        parent = node["parent"]
        if parent is not None and (parent not in nodes or not isinstance(nodes[parent], dict) or nodes[parent].get("kind") != node["kind"]):
            raise ValueError("Missing preset parent.")
        if node["saved"].get("inherits", "") != (nodes[parent].get("name") if parent else ""):
            raise ValueError("Preset inheritance does not match its parent.")
        seen = {identity}
        while parent is not None:
            if parent not in nodes or parent in seen or not isinstance(nodes[parent], dict):
                raise ValueError("Missing or cyclic preset ancestry.")
            seen.add(parent)
            parent = nodes[parent].get("parent")
    reachable = set()
    for index, item in enumerate(selections):
        if not isinstance(item, dict) or not isinstance(item.get("node"), str) or item["node"] not in nodes or type(item.get("dirty")) is not bool:
            raise ValueError("Invalid selected preset.")
        node = nodes[item["node"]]
        kind = node["kind"] if individual else "machine" if index == 0 else "process" if index == 1 else "filament"
        slot = None if individual or index < 2 else index - 2
        if node["kind"] != kind or item.get("slot") != slot or isinstance(item.get("slot"), bool):
            raise ValueError("Invalid printer, process or filament order.")
        if not settings(item.get("effective")) or not settings(item.get("changes")) or not set(node["saved"]) <= set(item["effective"]):
            raise ValueError("Invalid captured edits.")
        if item["effective"].get("inherits", "") != node["saved"].get("inherits", ""):
            raise ValueError("Edited inheritance is unsupported.")
        if individual and (item["dirty"] or item["effective"] != node["saved"]):
            raise ValueError("Individual profiles must contain saved settings, without setup edits.")
        # Derive deltas ourselves; never trust file-provided import instructions.
        item["changes"] = {k: v for k, v in item["effective"].items() if k not in RUNTIME_ONLY and node["saved"].get(k) != v}
        at = item["node"]
        while at is not None and at not in reachable:
            reachable.add(at)
            at = nodes[at]["parent"]
    if reachable != set(nodes):
        raise ValueError("Setup contains unrelated presets.")
    return snapshot


def restore_user_directory(bundle, storage):
    root = next((p.parent for p in Path(storage).resolve().parents if p.name == "orca_plugins"), None)
    if root is None:
        raise ValueError("Could not locate Orca's preset directory.")
    users = (root / "user").resolve()
    for kind in ("machine", "process", "filament"):
        preset = getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind]).get_selected_preset()
        if preset.file:
            try:
                relative = Path(preset.file).resolve().relative_to(users)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if len(relative.parts) >= 3:
                return users / relative.parts[0]
    raise ValueError("Select a saved user printer or process preset before restoring.")


def prepare_restore(snapshot):
    """Pure planning; safe to run in a worker without live host handles or I/O."""
    bundle_id = "klippee-restore-" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]
    stages, expected = plan_import(snapshot, bundle_id, friendly=True)
    graph = import_graph(stages)
    return {"bundle_id": bundle_id, "stages": stages, "expected": expected,
            "ancestors": saved_expectations(snapshot, graph), "graph": graph,
            "names": [identity.split(":", 1)[1] for identity in expected], "nodes": len(graph),
            "profile": snapshot.get("format") == PROFILE_FORMAT,
            "kinds": [identity.split(":", 1)[0] for identity in expected]}


def restore_steps(plan, user, before, get_bundle, reload_local):
    """One audited file/native operation per tick; never retain a live host view."""
    local = user / "_local"
    bundle_id = plan["bundle_id"]
    if not local.resolve().is_relative_to(user.resolve()):
        raise ValueError("Orca's local preset directory points outside the active user folder.")
    local.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    for stage in plan["stages"]:
        target = local / stage["bundle_id"]
        if target.exists():
            raise ValueError("Restore name already exists. Review and retry.")
        for relative in stage["files"]:
            if not (target / relative).resolve().is_relative_to(target.resolve()):
                raise ValueError("Invalid restore path.")
            yield "Checking restore paths…"
    try:
        for stage in plan["stages"]:
            target = local / stage["bundle_id"]
            target.mkdir()
            yield "Creating separate preset copies…"
            for relative, content in stage["files"].items():
                path = target / relative
                path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                path.write_text(json.dumps(content, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2), encoding="utf-8")
                yield "Writing preset copies…"
        for stage in plan["stages"]:
            reload_local(stage["bundle_id"])
            yield "Loading restored presets…"
        for expected in (plan["expected"], plan["ancestors"]):
            for identity, settings in expected.items():
                bundle = get_bundle()
                failures = verify(bundle, {identity: settings}) + verify_graph(bundle, {identity: plan["graph"][identity]})
                del bundle
                if failures:
                    raise ValueError("Native settings verification failed.")
                yield "Checking restored settings and inheritance…"
        if capture(get_bundle()) != before:
            raise ValueError("The active setup changed during restore. Review and restore again.")
    except Exception as error:
        raise ValueError("Restore did not finish verification. Copies may remain under " + bundle_id + "; do not use them. Your original presets were not overwritten.") from error
    return {key: value for key, value in plan.items() if key != "stages"}


def restore_setup(snapshot, bundle, storage, reload_local):
    """Synchronous adapter for the disposable spike; the page advances ticks."""
    before = capture(bundle)
    steps = restore_steps(prepare_restore(snapshot), restore_user_directory(bundle, storage), before, lambda: bundle, reload_local)
    while True:
        try:
            next(steps)
        except StopIteration as done:
            return done.value


def remap_compatibility(config, snapshot, graph):
    """Retain original targets and add copied descendants explicitly.

    Orca 2.5 checks only the immediate printer parent, so translating a root
    name alone loses compatibility once capture adds another inheritance level.
    Never broaden an empty list or change a condition expression.
    """
    for key, kind in (("compatible_printers", "machine"), ("compatible_prints", "process")):
        value = config.get(key)
        if not value:
            continue
        targets = list(value) if isinstance(value, list) else next(csv.reader([value], delimiter=";", escapechar="\\"))
        additions = []
        for target in graph:
            if not target.startswith(kind + ":"):
                continue
            basename = target.rsplit("/", 1)[1]
            identity = None
            for original in snapshot["nodes"]:
                digest = hashlib.sha256(original.encode()).hexdigest()[:20]
                if basename.endswith("saved-" + digest):
                    identity = original
                    break
            while identity:
                node = snapshot["nodes"][identity]
                if node["name"] in targets:
                    additions.append(target.split(":", 1)[1])
                    break
                identity = node["parent"]
        additions = [name for name in additions if name not in targets]
        if additions:
            config[key] = targets + additions if isinstance(value, list) else value + ";" + ";".join(additions)
    return config


def plan_import(snapshot, bundle_id, friendly=False):
    """Build a new namespaced bundle, preserving the ancestry graph.

    Each selection gets a separate child of its captured saved preset. This
    retains both the saved state and explicit unsaved overrides, including the
    distinction when the same filament occurs in multiple slots.
    """
    if snapshot.get("format") not in (FORMAT, PROFILE_FORMAT):
        raise ValueError("Unsupported snapshot format")
    if not bundle_id or any(c not in "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-" for c in bundle_id):
        raise ValueError("Bundle id must contain lowercase letters, digits or hyphens")
    nodes = snapshot["nodes"]
    depths = {}

    def depth(identity, trail=()):
        if identity in trail:
            raise ValueError("Cyclic captured ancestry")
        if identity not in nodes:
            raise ValueError("Missing captured parent: " + identity)
        parent = nodes[identity]["parent"]
        if identity not in depths:
            depths[identity] = depth(parent, trail + (identity,)) + 1 if parent else 0
        return depths[identity]

    for identity in nodes:
        depth(identity)
    final_depth = max(depths.values()) + 1
    prefix = lambda level: "_local/" + bundle_id + "-d" + str(level) + "/"
    names = {identity: "saved-" + hashlib.sha256(identity.encode()).hexdigest()[:20]
             for identity in nodes}
    stages = [{"bundle_id": bundle_id + "-d" + str(level), "files": {}}
              for level in range(final_depth + 1)]
    expected = {}
    for stage in stages:
        stage["files"]["bundle_metadata.json"] = {
            "id": stage["bundle_id"], "name": "Klippee restored setup", "version": "1.1.0",
            "print_presets": [], "filament_presets": [], "printer_presets": []}
    list_keys = {"machine": "printer_presets", "process": "print_presets", "filament": "filament_presets"}

    def add(level, kind, name, document):
        document.update(name=name, type=kind, version="2.5.0.0", **{"from": "User"})
        files = stages[level]["files"]
        files[kind + "/" + name + ".json"] = document
        files["bundle_metadata.json"][list_keys[kind]].append(name)

    for identity, node in nodes.items():
        parent_id = node["parent"]
        if parent_id is not None and parent_id not in nodes:
            raise ValueError("Missing captured parent: " + parent_id)
        parent_config = nodes[parent_id]["saved"] if parent_id else {}
        document = deepcopy(node["source_json"]) if node["source_json"] is not None else {}
        # Project loading can put a filament override into the collection's
        # preset while its file still describes the old saved state. Reconcile
        # using the native effective delta, rather than exporting stale disk
        # values. Keep unknown source fields and retain source_json separately.
        document.update({key: value for key, value in node["saved"].items()
                         if key != "inherits" and key not in RUNTIME_ONLY
                         and parent_config.get(key) != value})
        document["inherits"] = prefix(depths[parent_id]) + names[parent_id] if parent_id else ""
        # Cloud identity is not valid for a newly-created local copy.
        for key in ("setting_id", "base_id", "user_id"):
            document.pop(key, None)
        add(depths[identity], node["kind"], names[identity], document)

    for index, selection in enumerate(snapshot["selections"]):
        identity = selection["node"]
        node = nodes[identity]
        name = "captured-" + str(index) + "-" + names[identity]
        if friendly:
            label = re.sub(r"[^a-zA-Z0-9._-]+", "-", node["name"]).strip(".-")[:70] or node["kind"]
            name = "restored-" + str(index) + "-" + label
        document = {"inherits": prefix(depths[identity]) + names[identity], **selection["changes"]}
        add(final_depth, node["kind"], name, document)
        config = deepcopy(selection["effective"])
        config["inherits"] = document["inherits"]
        expected[node["kind"] + ":" + prefix(final_depth) + name] = config
    graph = import_graph(stages)
    for stage in stages:
        for filename, document in stage["files"].items():
            if filename != "bundle_metadata.json":
                remap_compatibility(document, snapshot, graph)
    for config in expected.values():
        remap_compatibility(config, snapshot, graph)
    return stages, expected


def import_graph(stages):
    return {document["type"] + ":_local/" + stage["bundle_id"] + "/" + document["name"]:
            document["inherits"]
            for stage in stages for filename, document in stage["files"].items()
            if filename != "bundle_metadata.json"}


def verify_graph(bundle, graph):
    failures = []
    for identity, parent in graph.items():
        kind, name = identity.split(":", 1)
        collection = getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind])
        preset = collection.find_preset(name)
        if preset is None or preset.name != name:
            failures.append({"preset": name, "error": "ancestry node missing"})
        elif preset.config_value("inherits") != parent:
            failures.append({"preset": name, "error": "inheritance edge changed"})
        elif parent:
            ancestor = collection.find_preset(parent)
            if ancestor is None or ancestor.name != parent:
                failures.append({"preset": name, "error": "ancestor missing"})
    return failures


def saved_expectations(snapshot, graph):
    expected = {}
    for identity, node in snapshot["nodes"].items():
        basename = "saved-" + hashlib.sha256(identity.encode()).hexdigest()[:20]
        target = next(key for key in graph if key.startswith(node["kind"] + ":") and key.endswith("/" + basename))
        config = deepcopy(node["saved"])
        config["inherits"] = graph[target]
        expected[target] = remap_compatibility(config, snapshot, graph)
    return expected


def verify(bundle, expected):
    """Compare every exposed effective setting after the NATIVE host reload."""
    failures = []
    for identity, wanted in expected.items():
        kind, name = identity.split(":", 1)
        preset = getattr(bundle, COLLECTIONS[kind]).find_preset(name)
        if preset is None or preset.name != name:
            failures.append({"preset": name, "error": "not loaded"})
            continue
        actual = values(preset)
        # Preset identities are intentionally namespaced; these are not settings.
        for key in sorted(comparison_keys(actual, wanted)):
            if canonical_value(key, actual.get(key)) != canonical_value(key, wanted.get(key)):
                failures.append({"preset": name, "key": key,
                                 "expected": wanted.get(key), "actual": actual.get(key)})
    return failures


"""Save and restore isolated preset copies. Network work stays off the UI thread."""
from copy import deepcopy
import json
from pathlib import Path
from queue import Empty, Queue
import re
from threading import Thread, Event, Lock
from urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError
from urllib.parse import urlsplit
from urllib.request import HTTPRedirectHandler, HTTPHandler, HTTPSHandler, ProxyHandler, Request, build_opener
from http.client import HTTPConnection, HTTPSConnection
import socket
import os
import secrets
import uuid
import sys

from datetime import datetime, timezone


MAX_BYTES = 512_000


def sanitize_capture(snapshot):
    if snapshot.get("format") == "klippee-orca-library/v1":
        nodes, omitted = sanitize_capture({"nodes": snapshot["nodes"], "selections": []})
        current, current_omitted = sanitize_capture(snapshot["current"])
        return {**snapshot, "nodes": nodes["nodes"], "current": current}, sorted(set(omitted + current_omitted))
    omitted = set()

    def clean(value):
        if isinstance(value, dict):
            result = {}
            for key, item in value.items():
                if PRIVATE_KEY.search(key):
                    omitted.add(key)
                else:
                    result[key] = clean(item)
            return result
        if isinstance(value, list):
            return [clean(item) for item in value]
        return value

    # Only option keys are secrets; a preset name itself may contain "token".
    result = deepcopy(snapshot)
    for node in result["nodes"].values():
        node["saved"] = clean(node["saved"])
        node["source_json"] = clean(node["source_json"])
    for item in result["selections"]:
        item["effective"] = clean(item["effective"])
        item["changes"] = clean(item["changes"])
    return result, sorted(omitted)


def parse_connection(code):
    if not isinstance(code, str) or len(code) > 2048:
        raise ValueError("Paste the connection code from Klippee's Orca Workspace.")
    url = urlsplit(code.strip())
    local = url.hostname in {"localhost", "127.0.0.1", "::1"}
    if (url.scheme != "https" and not (url.scheme == "http" and local)) or not url.hostname or url.username or url.password or url.query or url.path not in {"", "/"}:
        raise ValueError("Use a connection code from an HTTPS Klippee site.")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"klorca_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}", url.fragment):
        raise ValueError("Connection code is incomplete. Copy it again from Klippee.")
    return url.scheme + "://" + url.netloc, url.fragment


class DisconnectedError(ValueError):
    pass


def saved_connection_path():
    return Path(orca.host.plugin.storage()) / "library-connection.json"


def store_connection(origin, token):
    # SDK-owned private plugin storage; never presets, page JS, or a restore receipt.
    path = saved_connection_path()
    temporary = path.with_suffix(".tmp")
    with open(temporary, "w", encoding="utf-8", opener=lambda name, flags: os.open(name, flags, 0o600)) as file:
        json.dump({"origin": origin, "token": token}, file)
    temporary.replace(path)


def load_connection():
    path = saved_connection_path()
    if not path.is_file():
        return None
    if path.stat().st_size > 4096:
        raise ValueError("Saved connection is invalid. Disconnect and connect again.")
    data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    origin, _ = parse_connection(data["origin"] + "/#klorca_" + "x" * 43)
    token = data["token"]
    if not isinstance(token, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"klorcadevice_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}", token):
        raise ValueError("Saved connection is invalid. Disconnect and connect again.")
    return origin, token


class NoRedirect(HTTPRedirectHandler):
    def redirect_request(self, request, fp, code, message, headers, newurl):
        raise ValueError("Klippee redirected the request. Create a code at the site's final address.")


class RequestLease:
    """Cancel socket I/O without waiting on a worker or a buffered-reader lock."""
    def __init__(self):
        self.stopped = Event()
        self.lock = Lock()
        self.connection = None

    def check(self):
        if self.stopped.is_set():
            raise ValueError("Request cancelled.")

    def attach(self, connection):
        # urllib can close its socket object while HTTPResponse still owns a
        # file reference. Keep an independent raw descriptor for cancellation,
        # including HTTPS (SSLSocket.dup itself is intentionally unsupported).
        borrowed = socket.socket(connection.family, connection.type, connection.proto, fileno=connection.fileno())
        try:
            borrowed.settimeout(connection.gettimeout())
            controller = borrowed.dup()
        finally:
            borrowed.detach()
        with self.lock:
            self.connection = controller
        if self.stopped.is_set():
            self.cancel()
        self.check()

    def cancel(self):
        self.stopped.set()
        with self.lock:
            connection, self.connection = self.connection, None
        if connection is not None:
            try:
                connection.shutdown(socket.SHUT_RDWR)
            except OSError:
                pass
            connection.close()

    def release(self):
        with self.lock:
            connection, self.connection = self.connection, None
        if connection is not None:
            connection.close()


def make_request(origin, token, path, payload):
    body = json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False).encode("utf-8")
    limit = 8_000_000 if path == "/api/orca/library" else MAX_BYTES
    if len(body) > limit:
        raise ValueError("Profile library is too large (maximum 8 MB)." if limit > MAX_BYTES else "Setup is too large (maximum 512 KB).")
    return Request(origin + path, data=body, method="POST", headers={
        "Authorization": "Bearer " + token, "Content-Type": "application/json", "Accept": "application/json",
        "User-Agent": "Klippee-OrcaSlicer/1.6.0 (+https://klippee.xyz)",
    })


def send_request(request, lease=None):
    lease = lease or RequestLease()
    # No redirects or environment proxies: permission applies to this exact URL.
    class CancellableConnection:
        def connect(self):
            lease.check()
            super().connect()
            lease.attach(self.sock)
        def send(self, data):
            lease.check()
            return super().send(data)
    class Http(CancellableConnection, HTTPConnection):
        pass
    class Https(CancellableConnection, HTTPSConnection):
        pass
    class HttpHandler(HTTPHandler):
        def http_open(self, req):
            return self.do_open(Http, req)
    class HttpsHandler(HTTPSHandler):
        def https_open(self, req):
            return self.do_open(Https, req, context=self._context)
    try:
        lease.check()
        with build_opener(NoRedirect(), ProxyHandler({}), HttpHandler(), HttpsHandler()).open(request, timeout=12) as response:
            limit = 1_000_000 if request.full_url.endswith("/restore/library") else 600_000 if request.full_url.endswith("/restore/profile") else 65_536
            raw = response.read(limit + 1)
            lease.check()
            if len(raw) > limit:
                raise ValueError("Klippee returned an oversized response.")
            return json.loads(raw)
    except HTTPError as error:
        if error.code == 401 and any(path in request.full_url for path in ("/api/orca/restore/", "/api/orca/device/")):
            raise DisconnectedError("This Orca connection expired or was disconnected. Connect again in Klippee.") from None
        if error.code == 401 and any(request.full_url.endswith(path) for path in ("/api/orca/library", "/api/orca/capture")):
            raise ValueError("This upload review expired or was cancelled. Review again in the plugin before saving.") from None
        if error.code in {400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 413, 429}:
            try:
                message = json.loads(error.read(4096)).get("error")
                if isinstance(message, str) and len(message) <= 300:
                    raise ValueError(message) from None
            except (json.JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError):
                pass
        raise ValueError("Klippee could not complete the request. Try again.") from None
    except (URLError, TimeoutError, OSError):
        raise ValueError("Could not reach Klippee. Check your connection and retry.") from None
    finally:
        lease.release()


def request_json(origin, token, path, payload):
    return send_request(make_request(origin, token, path, payload))


def selection_summary(snapshot):
    return [{"name": snapshot["nodes"][item["node"]]["name"], "kind": snapshot["nodes"][item["node"]]["kind"],
             "slot": item["slot"], "dirty": item["dirty"]} for item in snapshot["selections"]]


def validate_restore_document(document):
    snapshot = validate_restore(document)
    snapshot, _ = sanitize_capture(snapshot)
    snapshot = validate_restore({"snapshot": snapshot})
    plan_import(snapshot, "klippee-restore-preview", friendly=True)
    return snapshot


def validate_library_profile(document, identity):
    snapshot = validate_restore_document(document)
    if snapshot["format"] != PROFILE_FORMAT or snapshot["selections"][0]["node"] != identity:
        raise ValueError("Klippee returned a different profile. Reload the library and choose again.")
    return snapshot


def validate_library_listing(data):
    if not isinstance(data, dict) or "expiresAt" not in data or data["expiresAt"] is not None and not isinstance(data["expiresAt"], str):
        raise ValueError("Klippee returned an invalid library response.")
    if data["expiresAt"] is not None:
        expires = datetime.fromisoformat(data["expiresAt"].replace("Z", "+00:00"))
        if expires.tzinfo is None or expires <= datetime.now(timezone.utc):
            raise ValueError("Browse access expired. Create a new code in Klippee.")
    library = data.get("library")
    if library is None:
        return {"id": "", "profiles": [], "expiresAt": data["expiresAt"], "uploadsEnabled": data.get("uploadsEnabled") is True}
    if not isinstance(library, dict) or not isinstance(library.get("id"), str) or not isinstance(library.get("profiles"), list) or len(library["profiles"]) > 768:
        raise ValueError("Klippee returned an invalid profile list.")
    profiles = []
    for profile in library["profiles"]:
        if not isinstance(profile, dict) or profile.get("kind") not in {"machine", "process", "filament"} or not isinstance(profile.get("name"), str) or not 1 <= len(profile["name"]) <= 512 or profile.get("id") != profile["kind"] + ":" + profile["name"]:
            raise ValueError("Klippee returned an invalid profile identity.")
        profiles.append({key: profile.get(key) for key in ("id", "kind", "name", "nozzle", "parent", "custom")})
    if len({p["id"] for p in profiles}) != len(profiles):
        raise ValueError("Klippee returned duplicate profiles.")
    return {"id": library["id"], "profiles": profiles, "expiresAt": data["expiresAt"], "uploadsEnabled": data.get("uploadsEnabled") is True}


try:
    import orca
except ImportError:
    orca = None

if orca is not None:
    PAGE = globals().get("_KLIPPEE_PAGE") or Path(__file__).with_name("klippee_plugin.html").read_text(encoding="utf-8")

    class KlippeeCapture(orca.pages.PagesPluginCapabilityBase):
        def __init__(self):
            super().__init__()
            self.results = Queue()
            self.busy = False
            self.preview = None
            self.pending_upload = None
            self.connection = None
            self.browse_connection = None
            self.connection_loaded = False
            self.disconnecting = False
            self.browse_library = None
            self.browse_requested = None
            self.restore_preview = None
            self.restore_baseline = None
            self.restore_result = None
            self.loaded = True
            self.stop_work = Event()
            self.worker = None
            self.lease = None
            self.steps = None
            self.view = None
            self.notice = ""
            self.progress = ""
            self.title = ""

        def restored_message(self):
            result = self.restore_result
            return {"command": "restored", "names": result["names"], "nodes": result["nodes"], "profile": result.get("profile", False), "kinds": result.get("kinds", [])}

        def read_restore_receipt(self):
            path = Path(orca.host.plugin.storage()) / "latest-restore.json"
            if not path.is_file() or path.stat().st_size > 2_000_000:
                raise ValueError("Restore a setup first, then check your selected presets.")
            receipt = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            snapshot = validate_restore({"snapshot": receipt["snapshot"]})
            snapshot, _ = sanitize_capture(snapshot)
            stages, expected = plan_import(snapshot, receipt["bundle_id"], friendly=True)
            graph = import_graph(stages)
            self.restore_result = {"names": [key.split(":", 1)[1] for key in expected], "nodes": len(graph),
                                   "graph": graph, "expected": expected, "ancestors": saved_expectations(snapshot, graph),
                                   "profile": snapshot.get("format") == PROFILE_FORMAT, "kinds": [key.split(":", 1)[0] for key in expected]}

        def get_name(self):
            return "Klippee"

        def get_ui(self):
            return PAGE

        def publish(self, message):
            if not self.loaded:
                return
            if message["command"] == "error":
                self.notice = message["error"]
            elif message["command"] == "working":
                self.progress = message["text"]
                self.notice = ""
            else:
                self.view = message
                self.notice = ""
            self.post_message(message)

        def on_unload(self):
            self.loaded = False
            self.stop_work.set()
            if self.lease is not None:
                self.lease.cancel()
            self.lease = None
            self.worker = None
            if self.steps is not None:
                self.steps.close()
            self.steps = None
            self.busy = False
            self.pending_upload = None
            self.preview = self.connection = self.restore_preview = self.restore_baseline = None
            self.view = None
            self.browse_connection = self.browse_library = self.browse_requested = None
            self.restore_result = None
            self.restore_namespace = ""
            self.title = ""
            while not self.results.empty():
                try:
                    self.results.get_nowait()
                except Empty:
                    break

        def on_load(self):
            self.connection_loaded = False
            self.loaded = True
            self.stop_work = Event()

        def start_work(self, function, command):
            stop = self.stop_work = Event()
            queue = self.results
            self.busy = True
            def work():
                try:
                    data = function()
                    result = {"command": command, "data": data}
                except DisconnectedError as error:
                    result = {"command": "error", "error": str(error), "disconnected": True}
                except ValueError as error:
                    result = {"command": "error", "error": str(error)}
                except Exception:
                    result = {"command": "error", "error": "Operation failed. Check Orca's plugin permissions and retry."}
                result["_job"] = stop
                if not stop.is_set():
                    queue.put(result)
            self.worker = Thread(target=work, daemon=True)
            try:
                self.worker.start()
            except Exception:
                self.busy = False
                raise

        def start_request(self, origin, token, path, payload, command):
            request = make_request(origin, token, path, payload)
            # Orca's audit context is thread-local. Emit the standard urllib
            # audit event HERE, in the host callback, before any worker/DNS/I/O.
            # A native PermissionError aborts the action before a thread exists.
            sys.audit("urllib.Request", request.full_url, request.data, dict(request.headers), request.get_method())
            self.lease = RequestLease()
            lease = self.lease
            self.start_work(lambda: send_request(request, lease), command)

        def finish_restore(self, result):
            self.restore_result = result
            storage = Path(orca.host.plugin.storage())
            receipt = storage / "latest-restore.json"
            temporary = receipt.with_suffix(".tmp")
            temporary.write_text(json.dumps({"snapshot": self.restore_preview, "bundle_id": result["bundle_id"]}), encoding="utf-8")
            temporary.replace(receipt)
            (storage / "pending-restore.json").unlink(missing_ok=True)
            self.restore_preview = self.restore_baseline = None
            return self.restored_message()

        def check_steps(self):
            if self.restore_result is None:
                self.read_restore_receipt()
            result = self.restore_result
            selected = capture(orca.host.preset_bundle())
            names = [selected["nodes"][item["node"]]["name"] for item in selected["selections"]]
            failures = []
            for expected in (result["expected"], result["ancestors"]):
                for identity, settings in expected.items():
                    bundle = orca.host.preset_bundle()
                    failures += verify(bundle, {identity: settings}) + verify_graph(bundle, {identity: result["graph"][identity]})
                    del bundle
                    yield "Checking selected settings and inheritance…"
            if result.get("profile"):
                if capture(orca.host.preset_bundle()) != selected:
                    failures.append({"error": "Selection changed during verification"})
                if failures:
                    raise ValueError("Restored profile settings or inheritance no longer match the saved copy.")
                return {"command": "profile_verified", "nodes": result["nodes"]}
            for item, expected in zip(selected["selections"], result["expected"].values()):
                if any(canonical_value(key, item["effective"].get(key)) != canonical_value(key, expected.get(key))
                       for key in comparison_keys(item["effective"], expected)):
                    failures.append({"error": "Selected effective settings differ"})
            if capture(orca.host.preset_bundle()) != selected:
                failures.append({"error": "Selection changed during verification"})
            if names != result["names"] or failures:
                return {**self.restored_message(), "notice": "Select the printer, process and every filament slot listed below, then check again. Any current edits must match the restored copy."}
            return {"command": "restore_verified", "slots": len(names) - 2, "nodes": result["nodes"]}

        def advance(self):
            if self.steps is not None:
                try:
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": next(self.steps)})
                except StopIteration as done:
                    self.steps = None
                    self.busy = False
                    self.publish(self.finish_restore(done.value) if self.step_kind == "restore" else done.value)
                return
            while True:
                try:
                    result = self.results.get_nowait()
                except Empty:
                    return
                if result.pop("_job", self.stop_work) is self.stop_work:
                    break
            self.worker = None
            self.lease = None
            self.busy = False
            command = result["command"]
            if command == "upload_authorized":
                origin, token, scope = self.pending_upload
                self.pending_upload = None
                if result["data"].get("scope") != scope:
                    raise ValueError("Klippee returned a different upload review. Review again.")
                self.connection = (origin, token)
                if scope == "setup":
                    self.preview = sanitize_capture(capture(orca.host.preset_bundle()))
                command = "connected"
                result["command"] = command
            if self.disconnecting:
                self.disconnecting = False
                if command == "error":
                    result.update(disconnected=True, error="Disconnected on this computer. Klippee could not confirm server revocation; disconnect this installation in Klippee when online.")
            if result.get("disconnected"):
                saved_connection_path().unlink(missing_ok=True)
                self.browse_connection = self.browse_library = None
            if command == "device_paired":
                if result["data"].get("connected") is not True:
                    raise ValueError("Klippee did not confirm this connection. Connect again.")
                self.start_request(*self.browse_connection, "/api/orca/restore/library", {}, "library_listed")
                self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Connected. Loading your library…"})
                return
            elif command == "device_disconnected":
                result = {"command": "cancelled", "notice": "Disconnected from Klippee. Saved profiles are kept."}
            elif command == "library_listed":
                self.browse_library = validate_library_listing(result["data"])
                result = {"command": "library_listed", "library": self.browse_library, "origin": self.browse_connection[0]}
            elif command == "profile_downloaded":
                document = result["data"]
                identity = self.browse_requested
                self.start_work(lambda: validate_library_profile(document, identity), "restore_review_ready")
                self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Validating the saved profile and its full inheritance…"})
                return
            elif command == "restore_review_ready":
                self.restore_preview = result["data"]
                result = {"command": "restore_review", "selections": selection_summary(self.restore_preview),
                          "nodes": len(self.restore_preview["nodes"]), "omittedKeys": [],
                          "profile": self.restore_preview.get("format") == PROFILE_FORMAT}
            elif command == "restore_planned":
                plan = result["data"]
                self.restore_namespace = plan["bundle_id"]
                storage = Path(orca.host.plugin.storage())
                (storage / "pending-restore.json").write_text(json.dumps({"bundle_id": plan["bundle_id"]}), encoding="utf-8")
                self.steps = restore_steps(plan, self.restore_user, self.restore_baseline, orca.host.preset_bundle, orca.host.preset.bundles.reload_local)
                self.step_kind = "restore"
                self.busy = True
                self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Restoring preset copies…"})
                return
            elif command == "connected":
                library = result["data"].get("scope") == "library"
                if library:
                    self.preview = sanitize_capture(capture(orca.host.preset_bundle(), library=True))
                    profiles = self.preview[0]["profiles"]
                    result["profiles"] = [{**profile, "kind": self.preview[0]["nodes"][profile["node"]]["kind"],
                                           "name": self.preview[0]["nodes"][profile["node"]]["name"]} for profile in profiles]
                current = self.preview[0]["current"] if library else self.preview[0]
                result.update(selections=selection_summary(current), omittedKeys=self.preview[1],
                              nodes=len(self.preview[0]["nodes"]), origin=self.connection[0])
                self.title = (current["selections"][0]["node"].split(":", 1)[1] + " / " + current["selections"][1]["node"].split(":", 1)[1])[:120]
            elif command == "saved":
                self.connection = self.preview = None
                self.title = ""
            self.publish(result)

        def on_message(self, message):
            try:
                if isinstance(message, str):
                    message = json.loads(message)
                if not isinstance(message, dict):
                    return
                command = message.get("command")
                if not self.loaded:
                    return
                if command in {"poll", "ready"}:
                    self.advance()
                    if command == "ready":
                        if not self.connection_loaded:
                            self.connection_loaded = True
                            if not self.busy and not self.browse_connection:
                                self.browse_connection = load_connection()
                                if self.browse_connection:
                                    self.start_request(*self.browse_connection, "/api/orca/restore/library", {}, "library_listed")
                        pending = Path(orca.host.plugin.storage()) / "pending-restore.json"
                        if pending.is_file() and self.steps is None and not self.busy:
                            self.notice = "An earlier restore was interrupted. Unverified copies may remain; restore the saved file again before using new copies."
                        self.post_message({"command": "state", "busy": self.busy, "view": self.view,
                                           "notice": self.notice, "progress": self.progress, "title": self.title,
                                           "library": self.browse_library or ({"id": "", "profiles": [], "expiresAt": None} if self.browse_connection else None), "browseOrigin": self.browse_connection[0] if self.browse_connection else ""})
                    return
                if command == "set_title":
                    title = message.get("title")
                    if isinstance(title, str) and len(title) <= 120:
                        self.title = title
                    return
                if command == "disconnect_library":
                    connection = self.browse_connection or load_connection()
                    # Stop active work and erase local access even when offline.
                    self.on_unload()
                    self.loaded = True
                    self.stop_work = Event()
                    self.connection_loaded = True
                    saved_connection_path().unlink(missing_ok=True)
                    if connection and connection[1].startswith("klorcadevice_"):
                        self.disconnecting = True
                        self.publish({"command": "cancelled", "notice": "Disconnected on this computer. Disconnect this installation in Klippee too if the server cannot be reached."})
                        self.start_request(*connection, "/api/orca/restore/disconnect", {}, "device_disconnected")
                        self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Disconnecting… If offline, also disconnect this Orca installation in Klippee."})
                    else:
                        self.publish({"command": "cancelled", "notice": "Disconnected locally. Cancel the old browse code in Klippee to revoke it immediately."})
                    return
                if command == "cancel":
                    namespace = getattr(self, "restore_namespace", "")
                    saved_browse, saved_library = self.browse_connection, self.browse_library
                    self.on_unload()
                    self.loaded = True
                    self.stop_work = Event()
                    self.browse_connection, self.browse_library = saved_browse, saved_library
                    self.publish({"command": "cancelled", "library": saved_library, "origin": saved_browse[0] if saved_browse else "", "notice": ("Restore stopped. Unverified copies may remain under " + namespace + "; do not use them.") if namespace else "Cancelled locally. Your saved connection is kept. An upload already sent may still finish; reload Klippee to check." if saved_browse else "Cancelled locally. A save already sent may still finish; reload saved copies in Klippee."})
                    return
                if self.busy:
                    return
                if command in {"browse_library", "reload_library"}:
                    self.restore_preview = None
                    if command == "browse_library":
                        self.browse_library = None
                        origin, code = parse_connection(message.get("code"))
                        # Persist before sending so a lost response cannot lose a
                        # successfully paired credential. Never persist the code.
                        token = "klorcadevice_" + secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
                        store_connection(origin, token)
                        self.browse_connection = (origin, token)
                        self.connection_loaded = True
                        self.start_request(origin, code, "/api/orca/restore/pair", {"token": token}, "device_paired")
                        self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Connecting this Orca installation to Klippee…"})
                        return
                    if not self.browse_connection:
                        self.browse_connection = load_connection()
                    if not self.browse_connection:
                        raise ValueError("Paste a Browse in Orca code from Klippee first.")
                    self.start_request(*self.browse_connection, "/api/orca/restore/library", {}, "library_listed")
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Loading your Klippee library…"})
                elif command in {"review_saved_library", "review_saved_setup"}:
                    connection = self.browse_connection or load_connection()
                    if not connection or not connection[1].startswith("klorcadevice_"):
                        raise ValueError("Connect this Orca installation to Klippee first.")
                    self.browse_connection = connection
                    self.preview = self.connection = self.restore_preview = None
                    self.view = None
                    scope = "library" if command == "review_saved_library" else "setup"
                    token = "klorca_" + secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
                    self.pending_upload = (connection[0], token, scope)
                    self.start_request(*connection, "/api/orca/device/upload-connection", {"id": str(uuid.uuid4()), "token": token, "scope": scope}, "upload_authorized")
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Preparing your profile import review…" if scope == "library" else "Preparing your setup review…"})
                elif command == "review_library_profile":
                    library = self.browse_library
                    identity = message.get("profileId")
                    if not self.browse_connection or not library or not any(p["id"] == identity for p in library["profiles"]):
                        raise ValueError("Load the library and choose a profile first.")
                    if library["expiresAt"] is not None and datetime.fromisoformat(library["expiresAt"].replace("Z", "+00:00")) <= datetime.now(timezone.utc):
                        self.browse_connection = self.browse_library = None
                        raise ValueError("Browse access expired. Create a new code in Klippee.")
                    self.restore_preview = None
                    self.browse_requested = identity
                    self.restore_baseline = capture(orca.host.preset_bundle())
                    self.start_request(*self.browse_connection, "/api/orca/restore/profile", {"profileId": identity, "importId": library["id"]}, "profile_downloaded")
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Reading the saved profile and its ancestors…"})
                elif command == "review_restore":
                    self.view = None
                    self.restore_preview = None
                    self.preview = None
                    self.connection = None
                    text = message.get("text")
                    if not isinstance(text, str) or len(text.encode("utf-8")) > 600_000:
                        raise ValueError("Choose a Klippee profile or setup export smaller than 600 KB.")
                    self.restore_baseline = capture(orca.host.preset_bundle())
                    self.start_work(lambda: validate_restore_document(json.loads(text)), "restore_review_ready")
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Validating saved setup…"})
                elif command == "restore" and self.restore_preview:
                    bundle = orca.host.preset_bundle()
                    if capture(bundle) != self.restore_baseline:
                        self.restore_preview = None
                        raise ValueError("Your current setup changed. Review the saved profile or setup again before restoring.")
                    self.restore_user = restore_user_directory(bundle, orca.host.plugin.storage())
                    del bundle
                    snapshot = self.restore_preview
                    self.start_work(lambda: prepare_restore(snapshot), "restore_planned")
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Preparing restored copies…"})
                elif command == "check_restore":
                    self.steps = self.check_steps()
                    self.step_kind = "check"
                    self.busy = True
                    self.publish({"command": "working", "text": "Checking restored setup…"})
                elif command == "review":
                    self.view = None
                    self.connection = None
                    self.preview = None
                    connection = parse_connection(message.get("code"))
                    snapshot = capture(orca.host.preset_bundle())
                    self.preview = sanitize_capture(snapshot)
                    self.connection = connection
                    self.start_request(*connection, "/api/orca/capture/context", {}, "connected")
                elif command == "save" and self.preview and self.connection:
                    library = self.preview[0].get("format") == "klippee-orca-library/v1"
                    current = sanitize_capture(capture(orca.host.preset_bundle(), library=library))
                    if current != self.preview:
                        self.preview = None
                        raise ValueError("The setup changed after review. Review it again before saving.")
                    title = message.get("title")
                    if not isinstance(title, str) or not title.strip() or len(title) > 120:
                        raise ValueError("Give this setup a name (up to 120 characters).")
                    info = orca.host.app_info()
                    self.start_request(*self.connection, "/api/orca/library" if library else "/api/orca/capture", {
                        **({"library": self.preview[0]} if library else {"snapshot": self.preview[0]}),
                        "title": title.strip(), "omittedKeys": self.preview[1],
                        "hostVersion": info["version"], "hostBuild": info["build"],
                    }, "saved")
            except PermissionError:
                self.busy = False
                self.steps = None
                if self.disconnecting:
                    self.disconnecting = False
                    self.publish({"command": "error", "disconnected": True, "error": "Disconnected on this computer. Orca denied the server revocation request; disconnect this installation in Klippee too."})
                else:
                    self.publish({"command": "error", "error": "Orca denied permission. No new network request was started. Check the requested access before retrying."})
            except ValueError as error:
                self.busy = False
                self.steps = None
                self.publish({"command": "error", "error": str(error)})
            except Exception:
                self.busy = False
                self.steps = None
                self.publish({"command": "error", "error": "Could not complete the setup action. Check the file and Orca's plugin permissions, then retry."})

    @orca.plugin
    class KlippeePlugin(orca.base):
        def register_capabilities(self):
            orca.register_capability(KlippeeCapture)
